      "titre": "Can / could : la capacité et la demande polie",
      "explication": "Can exprime la capacité (I can read Chinese. / I can't come.) et la permission (Can I open the window?). Pour demander la permission : Can + I + base verbale ? Pour demander un service poliment : Could + you + base verbale ? Could est plus poli que can.",
      "exemples": [
        "Can you read Chinese?",
        "I'm sorry, I can't.",
        "Can I go to the toilets?",
        "Could you open the window, please?"
